// The workspace lists every Go module in this repository: the shared root and
// the four services that import it. It is committed on purpose.
//
// What it buys: ONE build list for all five modules. Without a workspace each
// module resolves its dependencies independently -- `hub` could sit on
// golang.org/x/sys v0.47.0 while `rx` builds against v0.29.0 and nothing says
// so. Here they share one resolution, and `go work sync` writes that shared
// build list back into each go.mod, which is why adopting this file also bumped
// x/sys in the four modules that had drifted. It also makes the workspace-wide
// patterns work: `go build all`, `go vet all` and `go list all` see all 32
// packages across the five modules.
//
// What it does NOT do: `go build ./...` at the repository root still covers only
// the root module's 8 packages. A nested module is never matched by `./...`,
// workspace or not -- `./...` is a filesystem pattern that stops at every
// go.mod. Use `all` for a whole-repo sweep, or the per-module loop in the
// Makefile.
//
// What it does NOT replace: the `replace github.com/booleanism/surr => ../`
// directives in the four service go.mod files stay. A workspace only applies
// while you are inside it -- `GOWORK=off` (what a consumer, or a CI job that
// ignores the workspace, sees) must still resolve the shared module, and the
// only thing that makes it resolvable is the replace, because
// `github.com/booleanism/surr` is not published. Dropping them breaks
// `GOWORK=off go build` with "missing go.sum entry needed to verify package ...
// is provided by exactly one module" and `go mod tidy` with "repository
// 'https://github.com/booleanism/surr/' not found". If the module is ever pushed
// to a real remote and tagged, the replaces can go and this workspace becomes
// the only thing pointing at the local tree -- until then both mechanisms are
// load-bearing and neither is redundant.
//
// Keep the list in step: a module missing here is silently built against its own
// `replace`d copy instead of the working tree.

go 1.27.1

use (
	.
	./analytics
	./hub
	./rx
	./subscriptions
	./tx
)
